WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:14.780
Hank frowned at the sketch on his desk.

2
00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:21.462
His class was having a T-shirt contest for Earth Day, and each student had to create a logo.

3
00:00:21.463 --> 00:00:26.277
Then Mrs. Getty would choose a winner and order T-shirts for everyone.

4
00:00:26.278 --> 00:00:31.368
Hank had sketched a green frog with a speech bubble that read Think Green.

5
00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:34.882
But he didn't like his design very much.

6
00:00:34.883 --> 00:00:41.574
He added a superhero cape and a new speech bubble: Fight for Earth.

7
00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:47.000
"That's better," he thought. "But—"

8
00:00:47.001 --> 00:00:52.352
Anna suddenly poked him with her pencil.

9
00:00:52.353 --> 00:00:55.683
"Cool logo," she whispered.

10
00:00:55.684 --> 00:01:01.332
"Thanks." Hank was still frowning. "I don't like it."

11
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:04.359
"I do. I hate to draw and—"

12
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.392
"Anna and Hank!" Mrs. Getty said sharply.

13
00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:13.734
"You're supposed to be writing book reviews—not talking."

14
00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:16.890
"Sorry," Hank mumbled.

15
00:01:16.891 --> 00:01:21.088
"It's time for math now," the teacher said to the class.

16
00:01:21.089 --> 00:01:25.129
"You can finish your reviews later—for homework."

17
00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.318
Everyone groaned.

18
00:01:29.319 --> 00:01:35.184
As Hank flipped his notebook closed, a burst of air sent papers flying off his desk.

19
00:01:35.185 --> 00:01:39.436
Sighing, he scooped them up.

20
00:01:39.437 --> 00:01:41.963
"Ugh," he thought.

21
00:01:41.964 --> 00:01:45.125
He hadn't even finished reading his book yet.

22
00:01:45.126 --> 00:01:49.979
Writing this dumb book review would take forever.

23
00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:57.144
Hank started his homework right after dinner, but as he read, his thoughts kept drifting to the T-shirt contest.

24
00:01:57.145 --> 00:02:01.261
"I'll just draw for a few minutes," he thought.

25
00:02:01.262 --> 00:02:03.977
"Then I'll finish reading."

26
00:02:03.978 --> 00:02:07.896
Hank quickly sketched some ideas.

27
00:02:07.897 --> 00:02:14.707
Next he used colored pencils to add color and details to several designs.

28
00:02:14.708 --> 00:02:19.778
He didn't notice the time until his phone suddenly beeped.

29
00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:22.338
"Ack!" he cried.

30
00:02:22.339 --> 00:02:25.881
"My book review! I lost track of time!"

31
00:02:25.882 --> 00:02:29.545
Hank reached for his phone.

32
00:02:29.546 --> 00:02:34.529
Before he could stop himself, he searched the internet for the title of his book.

33
00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:42.211
A link popped up, which took him to a website . . . with hundreds of book reviews.

34
00:02:42.212 --> 00:02:45.342
"Perfect," he whispered.

35
00:02:45.343 --> 00:02:53.190
He began copying a review into his notebook, and fifteen minutes later his homework was done.

36
00:02:53.191 --> 00:02:58.056
On Friday afternoon Mrs. Getty stood at the front of the room.

37
00:02:58.057 --> 00:03:02.466
"It's time to announce our contest winner."

38
00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:05.659
"Yes!" Hank pumped his fist.

39
00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:11.686
"All the designs are wonderful." She flashed a smile at Hank.

40
00:03:11.687 --> 00:03:14.883
"Some are very elaborate.

41
00:03:14.884 --> 00:03:18.894
But I chose one that will work well on a T-shirt.

42
00:03:18.895 --> 00:03:22.977
The winner is . . . Anna!"

43
00:03:22.978 --> 00:03:29.395
"Anna?" Hank gasped as Mrs. Getty held up Anna's design.

44
00:03:29.396 --> 00:03:34.360
"Huh?" Hank blinked.

45
00:03:34.361 --> 00:03:38.647
Anna's logo was a frog in a superhero cape!

46
00:03:38.648 --> 00:03:42.669
At recess Hank stalked over to Anna.

47
00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:45.996
"You stole my design!"

48
00:03:45.997 --> 00:03:48.535
Anna's face turned red.

49
00:03:48.536 --> 00:03:55.273
"I'm sorry, Hank! Your sketch fell on the floor, and you said you didn't like it. So—"

50
00:03:55.274 --> 00:03:59.206
"So you stole it!" Hank snapped.

51
00:03:59.207 --> 00:04:02.085
"Don't you know it's wrong to steal other people's ideas?

52
00:04:02.085 --> 00:04:05.740
It's called plagiarism!"

53
00:04:05.741 --> 00:04:11.392
Anna bit her lip. "I'll tell Mrs. Getty after recess."

54
00:04:11.393 --> 00:04:13.319
"Good!"

55
00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:19.007
When they got back to the classroom, Anna started slowly toward the teacher.

56
00:04:19.008 --> 00:04:23.504
Hank watched her.

57
00:04:23.505 --> 00:04:29.814
"I'm glad Mrs. Getty will find out that I designed that logo," he thought.

58
00:04:29.815 --> 00:04:36.055
Just then his eyes landed on his notebook, and he felt a jolt.

59
00:04:36.056 --> 00:04:40.389
"I stole someone's ideas too," he realized.

60
00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:44.316
"I plagiarized my book review."

61
00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:48.109
Hank stood up, grabbing his notebook.

62
00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:53.780
He needed to talk to Mrs. Getty too.
